# MODIFIED-ARROWS-SCREENS: a held arrow, and Ctrl-B and Ctrl-F, under the full
# transcript. fx v0.0.16's screen binds the plain arrows only (keyForAction,
# input_full_transcript_runtime.zig:156-178@481104fd); every Super, Alt, Ctrl
# and Shift arrow is a composer move (modifiedArrowAction,
# escape_parser.zig:73-108), and Ctrl-B and Ctrl-F are bytes its keyForByte
# does not bind (:147-154). Each goes on to the composer behind the screen
# (app_input_runtime.zig:930, :872, :997-1001) and moves the caret there.
# p5-transcript-md's answer makes the document taller than the screen; a
# four-row draft waits, the caret at the end of its last row, `f`, one cell
# in. Each key on its own, each followed by Escape and a letter typed where
# the caret is: Super-Left (`Y`: the row's start, where fx's jump to the
# line's start and xfx's one-cell step land alike), Ctrl-Up (`X`: the row
# above, one cell in), Ctrl-B (`W`: one cell left), Ctrl-F (`V`: one right).
gateway p5-transcript-md-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
env TZ=UTC
wait 4
type show me the list
wait 1
key Enter
wait 12
snap answered
type one
key C-j
type two
key C-j
type three
key C-j
type f
wait 0.5
snap draft
key C-o
wait 2
snap full
key -H 1b 5b 31 3b 39 44
wait 1
snap full-super-left
key Escape
wait 1
type Y
wait 0.5
snap typed
key C-o
wait 2
key -H 1b 5b 31 3b 35 41
wait 1
snap full-ctrl-up
key Escape
wait 1
type X
wait 0.5
snap typed2
key C-o
wait 2
key -H 02
wait 1
snap full-ctrl-b
key Escape
wait 1
type W
wait 0.5
snap typed3
key C-o
wait 2
key -H 06
wait 1
snap full-ctrl-f
key Escape
wait 1
type V
wait 0.5
snap typed4
gwlog
